.TH UPDATECONF 1 "2026-09-07" "@PROJECT_NAME@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
updateconf \- merge new package configuration files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B updateconf
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B updateconf
finds configuration files below \fB/etc\fR with the configured new-file suffix (normally \fB.@EPKGNEW_EXT@\fR), displays a unified diff against the current file, and interactively lets the administrator update, discard, edit, or keep both files. It requires root privileges.
.PP
If the current file does not exist, the new file is removed. Identical files are also removed automatically.
.SH INTERACTIVE ACTIONS
.TP
.B U
Replace the current file with the new file.
.TP
.B D
Discard the new file.
.TP
.B E
Edit the current file using \fBEDITOR\fR.
.TP
.B K
Keep both files.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B EDITOR
Editor used by the \fBE\fR action; defaults to \fBvim\fR.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero on completion or when no new files are present; non-zero if root access or the selected editor is unavailable.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pkgadd (1),
.BR @PROJECT_NAME@.conf (5)
